    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-99075",
      "summary": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrust_binder: reschedule node refcount update on thread exit\n\nWhen a thread exits via BINDER_THREAD_EXIT, its pending work items are\ncancelled. If a thread exits while holding a pending node refcount\nincrement (e.g. pushed as deferred work to that thread), the refcount\nincrement was previously dropped because Node::cancel() and\nNodeWrapper::cancel() were no-ops.\n\nDropping the refcount update leaves the node's delivery state and count\nstate desynchronized, and userspace will not receive the notification,\nwhich can cause the node to never be freed from the process's nodes tree\nwhen all external references are dropped.\n\nFix this by implementing DeliverToRead::cancel() for Node and NodeWrapper\nto move the pending refcount update to the process's work queue on thread\nexit so another thread can deliver it to userspace.",
      "cvssScore": null,
      "severity": "Unknown",
      "published": "2026-10-23",
      "modified": "2026-10-23",
      "cwe": null,
      "references": [
        "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-99075",
        "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a74ccd1bcc170e66525f34e9de8652b57e2cf3d",
        "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71cbad138969edecef01b28dff87d91b56db538d",
        "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fb0f8dfc5a030ed3d60a1d03acdc99c90ee99fc1"
      ],
      "vulnerableProducts": [],
      "isExploited": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-99080",
      "summary": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfs: Free any excess xarray nodes in clear_inode()\n\nFor many years we've had a hard to hit leak of xarray nodes.  Hugh\ndocumented it well in commit 786b31121a2c.  Recently people and\nsyzbot have found ways to force it to happen with madvise.  Rather\nthan fix the leaks where they happen, just call xa_destroy() which\nhas the side-effect of cycling the i_pages lock.",
      "cvssScore": null,
